    <section style="background:#fff; padding:60px 0;"><div class="container" style="max-width:900px; line-height:1.8; color:#475569; font-size:1.05rem;">
      <p style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">The Indian D2C market now exceeds $60 billion with 3,500+ brands competing across 19 categories. Getting verified video reviews from real consumers — not fake text reviews — is the competitive edge. Here are the best platforms for Indian brands in 2026.</p>
      <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem; font-weight:700; color:#1e293b; margin:2rem 0 1rem;">1. AnalyzeG — Best for Indian D2C Brands</h2>
      <p style="margin-bottom:1rem;"><strong>What it does:</strong> Face-presence verified 30-second in-hand video reviews with Power BI dashboards, sentiment analysis, and raw CSV/Excel export. Packages: 500 videos (₹5L), 1000 (₹9L), 1500 (₹12.75L). One-time pricing, no subscription.</p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;"><strong>Why it wins:</strong> Purpose-built for Indian D2C brands selling on Amazon India, Nykaa, Flipkart, or their own stores. 5-point verification prevents fakes at the source. 2-minute in-stock delivery. Raw video files include ad license for own-product videos.</p>
      <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem; font-weight:700; color:#1e293b; margin:2rem 0 1rem;">2. Bazaarvoice — Best for Enterprise Retail Syndication</h2>
      <p style="margin-bottom:1rem;"><strong>What it does:</strong> Enterprise UGC platform with syndication to Walmart, Target, Sephora, and 2,300+ retail sites. 13,000+ brands. Text, photo, and video reviews.</p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;"><strong>Limitation:</strong> Enterprise pricing ($20K-$100K+/yr). US/EU retail focus. Not designed for Indian D2C brands selling through own channels.</p>
      <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem; font-weight:700; color:#1e293b; margin:2rem 0 1rem;">3. Yotpo — Best for Shopify DTC Brands</h2>
      <p style="margin-bottom:1rem;"><strong>What it does:</strong> All-in-one eCommerce suite: reviews, loyalty, SMS, email. Shopify-native. Text and photo reviews with basic video.</p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;"><strong>Limitation:</strong> Shopify-dependent. Video is not the core product. No Power BI integration. No raw data export for non-Shopify channels.</p>
      <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem; font-weight:700; color:#1e293b; margin:2rem 0 1rem;">4. Trustpilot — Best for Company-Level Trust</h2>
      <p style="margin-bottom:1rem;"><strong>What it does:</strong> Open text review platform. Google star ratings. Company trust profiles.</p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;"><strong>Limitation:</strong> Text only — no video. Anyone can review (including competitors). No verification depth. No analytics dashboards.</p>
      <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem; font-weight:700; color:#1e293b; margin:2rem 0 1rem;">5. Reviews.io — Best Budget Option</h2>
      <p style="margin-bottom:1rem;"><strong>What it does:</strong> Text, photo, and basic video reviews. Rich snippets. Google/Facebook integration. SKU-level tagging. From $99/mo.</p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;"><strong>Limitation:</strong> Video is basic (add-on, not core). No face-presence verification. No Power BI. No raw data export.</p>
